From 9d9988a43e9e9ce9d3eff439a2dbb366dd587b2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:01:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): mask secret-flag values and bare tokens in
 holder descriptions

agent.redact masks known secret formats and a few flag names, so a holder
started with `--webhook-secret X`, `--signing-key=X`, `--auth X` or a bare
random token still showed it in full in doctor's (now uncut) holder list.
hermes_state_argv_secrets.mask_argv_secrets runs first on the argv: the
value after any flag whose name says key/token/secret/password/auth/
credential/cookie/bearer is masked whole, and so is a bare token that is
long, mixes letters and digits and has high entropy. Paths (they name where
a secret lives), URLs, hex (commits, UUIDs), Hermes ids and tokens with a
plain word segment are kept. Run over every live process on the Mac and on
example-gw, it masks only macOS's base64 service-descriptor arguments
besides real secrets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
